Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This repository contains no third-party source code, no model weights and no data.
The pipeline calls the components below at run time; each is obtained from its own
distributor and is governed by its own licence, which is not granted by this
repository's licence:

  * nnU-Net (Isensee et al.) — segmentation framework used to run both frozen
    segmentation networks.
  * DentalSegmentator (Dot et al.) — frozen 6-class CBCT segmentation network.
  * ToothFairy2 tooth segmentation network — frozen 33-class network used for the
    per-tooth anchors.
  * Qwen3.5-9B — the frozen language model that the LoRA adapters are trained on.
  * Qwen3-32B-AWQ — the local model used as the entailment judge during
    rejection-sampling fine-tuning and as the development scorer.
  * PubMedBERT sentence embeddings (neuml/pubmedbert-base-embeddings) — the frozen
    text encoder used as the anchor of the region-text alignment loss.
  * RadFact (Microsoft) and radfact_lite (AImageLab) — report-level scoring code.
  * PyTorch, Hugging Face transformers / PEFT / bitsandbytes, SimpleITK, and the other
    packages pinned in pyproject.toml.

